{"step_index":801,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:43:48Z","thinking":"**Capturing Python Output**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! `add_log` is now intercepting *all* `print()` statements from Python, even those originating deep within imported modules like `pdf_reader.py`. This means the user will see absolutely everything. Since `add_log` triggers `new_log` events that JavaScript appends to the `<textarea>`, we're getting total visibility.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add new_log listener to pipeline-log-terminal in progress widget","EndLine":1102,"Instruction":"Append logs to the pipeline-log-terminal too","ReplacementContent":"// Logs Logic\nwindow.addEventListener('new_log', function(e) {\n    // 1. Update the main system logs textarea\n    const logArea = document.getElementById('system-logs');\n    if (logArea) {\n        logArea.value += e.detail + '\\n';\n        logArea.scrollTop = logArea.scrollHeight;\n    }\n    \n    // 2. Update the floating widget terminal if it's visible\n    const progressModal = document.getElementById('progress-modal');\n    if (progressModal && progressModal.style.display === 'flex') {\n        const termEl = document.getElementById('pipeline-log-terminal');\n        if (termEl) {\n            const newLog = document.createElement('div');\n            newLog.innerText = e.detail;\n            termEl.appendChild(newLog);\n            termEl.scrollTop = termEl.scrollHeight;\n        }\n    }\n});","StartLine":1078,"TargetContent":"// Logs Logic\nwindow.addEventListener('new_log', function(e) {\n    const logArea = document.getElementById('system-logs');\n    if (logArea) {\n        logArea.value += e.detail + '\\n';\n        logArea.scrollTop = logArea.scrollHeight;\n    }\n});","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html","toolAction":"Hook pipeline terminal to real logs","tool